      {
        "trackId": "ok_clean_slate",
        "affectedElement": "governing_mechanism",
        "question": "Answered in the negative, and now dated. The Oklahoma State Bureau of Investigation has not launched the expedited request portal. Its criminal history record expungement page, last updated 23 July 2026 and therefore after the Act took effect, describes no portal and gives an email address and telephone number for enquiries. Section 19d(A) sets the deadline at 1 November 2026, which has not arrived, so this is a duty not yet due rather than a duty breached. It is carried forward as the portal-delivery monitor."
      },
      {
        "trackId": "ok_clean_slate",
        "affectedElement": "filing_process",
        "question": "What the § 19d(A) portal will require in practice once it is published: the § 19d(B) submission contents are stated in the statute, but the published procedure, the identity evidence and the turnaround are not."
      },
      {
        "trackId": "ok_clean_slate",
        "affectedElement": "governing_mechanism",
        "question": "Whether the funds on which 22 O.S. § 18b(B) conditions eligibility have been appropriated. The statute confers eligibility \"subject to the availability of funds\" and the Act makes no appropriation determinable from its own text. Until that is known, no participant may be told that the sealing-without-petition route will reach their record."
      },
      {
        "trackId": "ok_osbi_portal",
